  "rebindNote": "Eight pages were rebound on 2026-08-18 (marked `rebound`). The rule was provable, never approximate: a value matching a rung exactly binds that rung; a value >= half the shorter side binds shape/full, since it ALREADY renders fully rounded; 10 snaps to 12 by explicit decision; anything else was left and reported. Each page's authorable property COUNT is asserted unchanged before its numbers are accepted — a rebind that moves the count has done something other than rebind.",
  "chromeNote": "COMPONENT_SET radii were separated out on 2026-08-18 as class `chrome`. Figma draws a dashed wrapper around every variant set and gives it a DEFAULT 5px corner radius; it is editor chrome that renders in no product. It had been counted as a raw non-zero defect on 23 pages — 248 properties — which is why 5 was the single most persistent off-ladder value in the census and why it appeared on almost every page at once. VERIFIED DIRECTLY on nine pages (Inputs, Buttons, Iconography, Dropdown, Date-Time Picker, Stepper, Tabs, Footer, Carousel — 148 of the 248): in every one, 100 % of radius-5 sat on a COMPONENT_SET, none anywhere else, and COMPONENT_SET carried no value other than 5. The remaining 14 pages are inferred from that and will be confirmed on the next sweep; the ratchet catches it if the inference is wrong.",
  "coverageNote": "COMPLETE — all 69 pages censused as of 2026-08-18. `censusBefore` on the final 34 records the state at first measurement, so the census stands on its own even though those pages were rebound in the same pass.",
  "fractionalNote": "116 FRACTIONAL radii (4.800, 4.804, 3.900, 3.200, 2.925, 5.472, 8.030, 10.121 px) were bound to their NEAREST rung on 2026-08-18, every move under 1.1px and none visible. Two distinct causes, established by inspection rather than assumed: on Popover and Tabs the node dimensions are INTEGRAL (278x54, 145x98) — nothing was scaled, the radius was simply off-ladder. On New in 2.0 and Thumbnail the dimensions ARE fractional and the artwork genuinely was scaled. The earlier objection that binding would 'hide the scaling defect' was half wrong: Figma's scale tool bakes the radius as an ABSOLUTE value, so resizing the box does not restore it — the radius has to be set back either way. The fractional BOX is a separate, cosmetic issue, listed in fractionalBoxes.",
  "fractionalBoxes": {
    "note": "Nodes whose width/height are fractional — cosmetic, not a radius defect, and needs a designer rather than a script. Listed so it is not rediscovered as a mystery.",
